# The Gradle wrapper is committed on purpose. Flutter's template ignores it,
# but then a fresh clone cannot run ./gradlew, which CONTRIBUTING and CI both
# ask for, and everyone ends up on whichever Gradle their machine happens to
# have. Committing it is what Gradle itself recommends.
/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
